{"The `findMembers()` promise is discarded (fire-and-forget), introducing a race condition. The old `afterModel` hook returned the promise so Ember waited for members to load before rendering. Now the template renders immediately with no members, and if the user navigates away before the AJAX completes, the `.then` callback will still set properties on the (now stale) model.": 0.9059200882911682, "The `findMembers()` method caps `offset` at `user_count` (`Math.min(this.get(\"user_count\"), ...)`), which means if the offset equals the total user count, the request will return zero results \u2014 an empty last page. The cap should account for the limit.": 0.6093167066574097, "HTTP method mismatch: this test uses `:put` but the success-case test for the same `remove_member` action uses `:delete`. This test likely hits the wrong route and doesn't actually verify the automatic-group protection on the `remove_member` endpoint.": 0.973261833190918, "Wrong interpolation syntax for a client-side locale file. This file uses `{{variable}}` (Handlebars-style) for interpolation, but `%{variable}` (Ruby i18n style) is used here. The variables will render literally in the UI instead of being substituted.": 0.23753292858600616, "`totalPages` has an off-by-one bug; it should use ceiling division instead of `floor(...) + 1`.": 0.9089608788490295, "`group.users.delete(user_id)` passes a raw integer and bypasses `Group#remove`, which runs destroy callbacks that reset `primary_group_id`. Use the model's `remove` method with a User object, consistent with how `add_members` uses `group.add(user)`.": 0.8349514603614807, "Returning `undefined` instead of a resolved promise breaks the method's promise-based contract. The previous code returned `Ember.RSVP.resolve([])`, ensuring callers could safely chain `.then()`. Any future (or current) caller that chains on `findMembers()` will get a TypeError when the name is empty.": 0.932864248752594, "The remove control uses `<a>` without `href`, making it inaccessible via keyboard (not focusable). Use a `<button>` element instead, and add an `aria-label` so screen readers can identify the action.": 0.5106411576271057, "The `self.findMembers()` return value is not returned from the `.then()` callback, so the outer promise resolves before the member list reload completes. Any caller chaining on `removeMember()` won't know when members are actually reloaded.": 0.8439059257507324, "Negative `offset` (or `limit`) values will cause a PostgreSQL error and a 500 response. Clamp both to a minimum of 0.": 0.8383241891860962, "No upper bound on `limit` \u2014 a client can pass `?limit=999999` to bypass pagination entirely. Cap it to a reasonable maximum (e.g., 1000).": 0.7576913237571716, "Hardcoded hex colors `#333` and `#aaa` break theming. The rest of this file consistently uses SCSS variables like `$primary` for colors.": 0.49764207005500793, "The `for=\"alias\"` attribute on this label won't associate with the combo-box below because the component sets `name=\"alias\"` but not `id=\"alias\"`. Add `id=\"alias\"` to the combo-box.": 0.21764986217021942, "The `for=\"name\"` attribute on this label won't associate with the text-field below because the component sets `name=\"name\"` (HTML name attribute) but not `id=\"name\"`. Add `id=\"name\"` to the text-field to make the label clickable.": 0.3121410310268402, "Adding a form without a submit handler means pressing Enter in the name field will submit the browser form and reload the page. Attach a submit action (or prevent default) so the form doesn't navigate away.": 0.9717779755592346, "Use strict equality (`===`) instead of loose equality (`==`) to avoid subtle type-coercion issues.": 0.010629238560795784, "Stray semicolon after `}` creates an empty statement. The `;` should be either inside the braces (after `return`) or removed entirely.": 0.015603367239236832, "Inconsistent quote style: `\"model\"` uses double quotes while adjacent strings (`'group'`, `'members'`) use single quotes.": 0.07695196568965912}